.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-UPLOAD-DIRECTORY 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-upload-directory \- upload every file in a local directory to a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm upload-directory
.BR \-\-bucket\-ern | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-dir | \-d
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR|\fB\-r\fR]
[\fB\-\-part\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-concurrency\fR|\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uploads every file found under a local directory to a bucket, one
object per file. This is the batch counterpart to
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1);
each file uses the exact same single-request/multipart logic that
action does, chosen independently per file by its size relative to
.BR \-\-part\-size .
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-recursive ,
only files directly inside
.B \-\-dir
are uploaded; subdirectories and their contents are skipped. With
.BR \-\-recursive ,
the whole directory tree under
.B \-\-dir
is walked and every regular file found is uploaded.
.PP
Each object's key is
.B \-\-prefix
(empty by default) followed by the file's path relative to
.BR \-\-dir ,
with forward slashes regardless of platform - e.g. a file at
.I <dir>/sub/report.csv
becomes key
.I <prefix>sub/report.csv .
Files are uploaded in a deterministic order (sorted by path), one at a
time; within a single file's multipart upload, up to
.B \-\-concurrency
parts still run in parallel, same as
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1).
.PP
Processing continues after a single file fails, so one bad file
doesn't block the rest of the directory; the command's own exit status
reflects whether every file succeeded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the destination bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Local directory to upload. Required; the command fails immediately if
this is not a directory.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Prepended to every uploaded object's key, in front of the file's path
relative to \fB\-\-dir\fR. Optional; empty by default.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Walk subdirectories too, instead of only the top level of
\fB\-\-dir\fR.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-part\-size " " \fIBYTES\fR
Size threshold, in bytes, above which a file is uploaded as multipart
rather than in a single request - applied per file, same as
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1)
\&'s option of the same name. Defaults to \fI5242880\fR (5 MiB), or the
value of \fIeuclid.modules.storage.part-size\fR in the loaded
configuration file if set - see
.BR \-\-config
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-concurrency " " \fIN\fR
Number of parts to upload in parallel, for any file that goes the
multipart route. Defaults to \fI4\fR, or the value of
\fIeuclid.modules.storage.concurrency\fR in the loaded configuration
file if set; values less than \fI1\fR are treated as \fI1\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was uploaded; a JSON array is printed, one entry per file
.RI ( "{key, file, result}" ),
where
.I result
is that file's uploaded object metadata (the same shape
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1)
prints for a single file).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, \fB\-\-dir\fR is not a directory, or one or
more files failed to upload; the printed JSON array still contains one
entry per file, with
.RI ( "{key, file, error: true}" )
in place of
.I result
for each one that failed. Per-file errors are also printed to standard
error as they happen.
.SH EXAMPLES
Upload only the files directly inside a directory, keyed under a
prefix:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm upload-directory \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --dir ./reports --prefix 2026-08/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upload an entire directory tree, with higher per-file part
concurrency:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm upload-directory \e
    --bucket-ern ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --dir ./reports --prefix archive/ --recursive \e
    --part-size 8388608 --concurrency 8
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-download-bucket (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
